   "source": [
    "## Performance mechanisms and observations\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Causal attention mask:** blocks future characters from influencing next-character predictions.\n",
    "- **Residual connections and pre-LayerNorm:** support gradient flow and training stability.\n",
    "- **Dropout and AdamW weight decay:** regularize a small training subset.\n",
    "- **Gradient clipping:** limits unusually large updates.\n",
    "- **Mini-batches and AdamW:** make parameter updates efficient and adaptive.\n",
    "- **Validation loss and perplexity:** monitor generalization and compare settings.\n",
    "- **Tied input/output embeddings:** share parameters between token lookup and character prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The small subset and short training runs are designed for a practical demonstration. Generated text may be repetitive or inconsistent; the settings comparison changes both model size and epoch count, so it illustrates the combined effect rather than isolating one variable."
   ]
